model { extend basalt.deployment { metadata { constraint "Deployment backend acceptance counts direct and pooled runtime client backends per logical database only after desired runtime readiness. Unknown visibility is a failed observation; release-only signed readiness and boot revalidation precede the unchanged 90-second convergence window within a 270-second overall operation counted from the readiness receipt. The existing two-minute verifier wrapper reserves five seconds for retention and teardown. Readiness asks again every five seconds while it is refused with 409, 429 or a 5xx status, for up to 690 seconds: 330 for the controller object to adopt the uploaded code, then up to 360 for the controller to replace a running runtime that keeps refusing: its 60-second refusal bound, its 30-second stop grace, the 180-second startup budget and 90 seconds for its waits that carry no name. The wait is computed from the controller's own constants, so it follows them. Any other refusal fails at once. The receipt records how often readiness was refused, the last refusal, and whether the controller object had adopted the code." } } }
